[[file:Attribute damage icon.png|50px]]
'''Damage''' refers to the amount of damage each tear deals to [[enemy|enemies]], and is represented by a sword. As damage increases, the size of the tears increases as well. However, tear size is not always a direct indication of how much damage tears will do; for example, items like {{i|Dead Onion}} and {{I|Tropicamide}} increase tear size without increasing damage. Tears will grow and shrink when damage changes, but tears of a certain size do not have a specific damage value, and two tears of the same size (in two different runs) are likely to have different damage values.

== Effective Damage ==
The formula for damage is: <math display="block">\mathit{EffectiveDamage} = (\mathit{CharBaseDmg} \times \sqrt{\mathit{TotalDmgUps} \times 1.2 + 1} + \mathit{FlatDmgUps}) \times \mathit{Multipliers}</math>

where:
* CharBaseDmg = The character's base damage multiplied by their multiplier,
* TotalDmgUps = the total of all regular damage ups collected (not including special exceptions or damage multipliers),
* FlatDmgUps = the total of all damage ups that are excluded from the above (for example, {{t|Curved Horn}} or {{i|Ipecac}}), and
* EffectiveDmg = the approximate damage that can be expected per tear, or per 'tick' when using {{i|Brimstone}} or {{i|Technology 2}}.

This formula makes most damage upgrades less potent the more that Isaac has. For example, a {{i|Pentagram}} (+1 Damage) on Isaac would make his total damage 3.5 × (1 × 1.2 + 1)^0.5 = 3.5 × 1.48 = 5.19. Another Pentagram (+1+1) increases this to 6.45 (a 1.26 increase instead of a 1.69 increase). The higher a character's base damage, the more effective damage ups will be for that character. Flat damage modifiers and special adjustments like {{i|Polyphemus}} or {{i|Sacred Heart}} happen after the main formula.

=== Character Modifier ===
The ''character base damage'' is defined by a base number and a multiplier.
* {{C|Eve}}<sup>†</sup> and {{C|Tainted Magdalene}}: 0.75 × 3.50 = 2.625
* {{C|Jacob}}<sup>‡</sup>: 1.00 × 3.50 - 0.75 = 2.75
* {{C|Isaac}}, {{C|Magdalene}}, {{C|Samson}}, {{C|Lazarus}}, {{C|Lilith}}, {{C|The Lost}}, {{C|Apollyon}}, {{C|The Soul}}, {{C|Bethany}}, {{C|Tainted Isaac}}, {{C|Tainted Judas}}, {{C|Tainted ???}}, {{C|Tainted Samson}}, {{C|Tainted Lazarus}}, {{C|Tainted Lilith}}, {{C|Tainted Keeper}}, {{C|Tainted Apollyon}}, {{C|Tainted Bethany}}, and {{C|Tainted Jacob}}: 1.00 × 3.50 = 3.50
* {{C|Eden}} and {{C|Tainted Eden}}: 1.00 x 3.50 ± 1.0 = from 2.50 to 4.50
* {{C|???}}: 1.05 × 3.50 = 3.675
* {{C|Esau}}<sup>‡</sup>: 1.00 × 3.50 + 0.25 = 3.75
* {{C|Keeper}}, {{C|Cain}}, {{C|Tainted Cain}}, {{C|Tainted Eve}}, and {{dlc|nr}}{{C|Lazarus Risen}}: 1.20 × 3.50 = 4.20
* {{C|Judas}}: 1.35 × 3.50 = 4.725
* {{C|Azazel}}, {{C|The Forgotten}}, {{C|Tainted Azazel}}, {{C|Tainted Forgotten}}, and {{C|Dead Tainted Lazarus}}: 1.50 × 3.50 = 5.25
* {{dlc+|r}}{{C|Lazarus Risen}}: 1.40 × 3.50 = 4.90 (+0.5 damage after each death, 6.20 effective damage on the first death){{dlc-}}
* {{C|Tainted Lost}}: 1.30 × 3.50 = 4.55
* {{C|Black Judas}}: 2 × 3.50 = 7.00

<sup>†</sup>: {{I|Whore of Babylon}} has the unique effect of increasing Eve's damage modifier from 0.75 to 1.00 when active. This does not apply to other characters, however.<br/>
<sup>‡</sup>: Jacob and Esau have -0.75 and +0.25 flat damage, respectively: their base damage, as far as the damage formula is considered, is still 3.5 with a 1.0 multiplier.

=== Damage Multipliers ===
Some items multiply damage rather than simply adding to it. Damage multipliers (not to be confused with the aforementioned character-inherent base multiplier) do not simply multiply the character's damage once; the damage stat is constantly recalculated and the damage multipliers are multiplied with the end result. This means that if a character starts with 3.50 damage and gets a 2× multiplier, their effective damage will be 3.5×2 = 7.00. If an item that grants +1 damage is picked up, the character's effective damage will be 3.5×(1×1.2+1)^0.5×2 = 3.5×(2.2)^0.5×2 = 3.5×1.48×2 = 10.38, and not 7.00 + 1.

Most damage multipliers stack. For example, {{Dlc|nr}}{{i|Proptosis}} and {{i|Eve's Mascara}} both provide a 2× multiplier; picking up both will give a total multiplier of 4×. The exception to this is the 1.5× damage multipliers provided by {{i|Cricket's Head}}, {{i|Magic Mushroom}}, and the combination of {{i|Blood of the Martyr}} and {{i|The Book of Belial}}. These multipliers do not stack; for example, picking up both Cricket's Head and Magic Mushroom will result in an overall 1.5× multiplier rather than the expected 2.25×. Some damage multipliers may be applied to certain flat damage increases, while others will not; see [[Damage#The order that damage multipliers and flat damage are applied|the section on the order in which damage multipliers and flat damage are applied]] for more information.

=== Reverse Formula ===
Consequently, the reverse formula to determine your damage bonuses from the displayed value is <math display="block">\mathit{Bonus} = \frac{1}{1.2}\left[\left(\frac{\mathit{EffectiveDamage}/\mathit{Multipliers} - \mathit{FlatDmgUps}}{\mathit{CharBaseDmg}}\right)^2 - 1\right]</math>
''Multipliers'' is the product of all damage multipliers in effect.

